    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 2/2 passing).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` field so an owner returns `SILVER` when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise `BRONZE`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipTier` enum property (`SILVER`/`BRONZE`) to the `Owner` schema. The OpenAPI generator produces the `OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum` nested enum from this.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` computing the tier:\n   ```java\n   owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0\n       && owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank()\n       ? MembershipTierEnum.SILVER : MembershipTierEnum.BRONZE\n   ```\n\nThe existing `CountOwnerNamesakes` function already stamps `namesakeCount` on the owner at create time, so the value is available when the owner is later loaded and serialized. Both new acceptance tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) and the full suite pass.",
